module gunbc.plans.derived_types_keep_their_name

import std.dissolution { unbound_dissolution }
import gunbc.plan { Plan, PlanRetiresWhen, PlanIsAuthorityOnly }
import std.markdown { MarkdownBlock }
import gunbc.markdown_helpers { h2, h3, p, li, ul, ol, quote }

// Planning-only intention. It organises rulings that already exist; it does not add a ruling.
// It is the answer to the operator's 2026-11-19 question "I thought we were getting rid of
// aliases?": the where-refinement retirement IS ruled, a blanket "no aliases" is NOT, and the
// measured reason a refined/branded/aliased type is interchangeable with its base is the checker's
// own alias/refinement transparency, not a missing argument check.

fn derived_types_keep_their_name_body() -> List<MarkdownBlock> {
  [
    quote(blocks: [
      p(text: "**This plan is written as an intention** (`gunbc.design_argument::plans_are_intentions`). Work items live under the roadmap in `gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_authority` and name this intention; this plan does not list them."),
      p(text: "**Grounding:** `gunbc.design_ruling::where_refinements_retire_for_checked_constructors` (where-refinements leave the language, replaced by checked constructors returning Optional), `gunbc.design_ruling::nonemptiness_is_constructed_or_proved`, `gunbc.design_ruling::machine_width_composition_has_an_intersection_carrier` (Compose is an intersection carrier, not a transparent alias), `gunbc.design_ruling::literal_only_refinement_judgment_is_interim` (the interim literal admission the v2 cut will retire), `gunbc.design_argument::single_authority` (a second name for one concept is nicknaming), `gunbc.design_argument::replacement_migration` (the old authority ends in one motion at its root), `gunbc.design_argument::root_generalization` (whose failure example (a) is literally Type-alias identity), `gunbc.design_argument::closed_grounded_substrate`."),
      p(text: "**Honest scope:** there is NO blanket ruling that bans type aliases. What is ruled is the retirement of `where`-refinements. Nickname aliases are discouraged by `single_authority`, not forbidden. This intention refuses the *interchangeability* (a base value standing in for a derived type at a check), and retires the forms the rulings already name, while keeping the legitimate abbreviation and intersection forms (section 3)."),
    ]),
    h2(text: "1. Intention"),
    p(text: "**What:** a type that a declaration derives from another type by refinement, brand, or a bare name is not interchangeable with its base at a judgment the compiler makes. Passing a value whose type is the base into a position whose declared type is the derived type, or back, is decided by ONE inhabitance rule that has the symbol table in hand; it is never waved through because the two names collapse to a common head. `where`-refinements are gone from the language and a derived type is reached only through a checked constructor returning Optional or through carried evidence (`where_refinements_retire_for_checked_constructors`, `nonemptiness_is_constructed_or_proved`). A bare alias that only renames a kernel or scalar carrier is gone (a second name for one concept, `single_authority`). What survives as an alias is the legitimate kind: an abbreviation of a parameterized type, and the Compose/phantom intersection forms governed by `machine_width_composition_has_an_intersection_carrier`."),
    p(text: "**Why (operator, 2026-11-19):** the operator believed aliases were being removed. They are, but only in the ruled slice (the `where`-refinements), and nothing on the required path currently refuses a plain String reaching a `NonEmptyStr`, branded, or even `nominal_opaque` parameter. The guarantee the operators think they have -- that a name like `PathSegment` or `CommitSha` means something the checker enforces -- is not on the path that judges code."),
    h2(text: "2. The measured hole (the argument check is NOT the problem)"),
    p(text: "On the v1 seed CompileAccept path -- the path the required gate and `gunbc run --claim-run` use -- a probe suite (scratch, never committed; harness `gunbc.compile_diagnostic_census`, idiom of `test.claim.int_argument_at_nat_parameter_witness`) shows the general call-argument-vs-parameter check FIRES: an `Int` at a declared record parameter, a `String` variable at a declared record parameter, and an `Int` at a declared `String` parameter are each refused with a blocking row; the well-typed controls are clean. Every SAME-BASE derived type is silently accepted with ZERO blocking rows of any class:"),
    ul(items: [
      li(text: "a `String` variable at a `std.types` `NonEmptyStr` parameter (a `where string_non_empty` refinement) -- accepted, zero blocking rows;"),
      li(text: "a `String` variable at a branded `std.types` `PathSegment` (`NonEmptyStr where brand(\"PathSegment\")`) parameter -- accepted, zero blocking rows;"),
      li(text: "a `String` variable at a local bare nickname `type MyStr = String` parameter -- accepted (this is `v1.compiler.infer_env` `alias_identity_in_judgment` collapsing both to the head `String` and returning Inhabits);"),
      li(text: "a `String` variable at a local `type MySecret nominal_opaque = String` parameter -- accepted (the modifier parses; the nominal-correct control is clean), so even the nominal marker does not refuse the base at argument position on this path."),
    ]),
    p(text: "**Conclusion:** the String/NonEmptyStr interchangeability is the alias/refinement/nominal TRANSPARENCY inside `v1.compiler.infer` `declared_type_inhabitance`, NOT a missing general argument check. Bare nicknames are admitted by `alias_identity_in_judgment` (Inhabits); a base at a `where`-refinement is admitted by `refinement_inhabitance` returning Undecidable (`UndecidableRefinementIntroduction`), and Undecidable is not a blocking refusal at the application. This runs the probe that `gunbc.recurring_failure_mode::an_int_argument_inhabits_a_nat_parameter_at_typecheck` records as STATED OUT, OWNED BY Q4, a probe separating `alias_identity_in_judgment` from the terminal fall-through."),
    h2(text: "3. The population to be cut apart, and what stays"),
    p(text: "Bounded grep over `dag/` and `src/v2/` (header lines beginning `type `), not a census; per-class counts, specimens, and the unknowns are recorded in section 7. Roughly:"),
    ul(items: [
      li(text: "(a) `where`-refinements, ruled to retire: about 326 headers, of which about 284 carry `brand(...)` (PathSegment, RunKey, LeaseToken, IntentId, ArtifactId, the `Int where range(...) brand(...)` widths, ...) and about 42 are pure predicates (`type Port = Int where range(...)`, `NonEmptyStr = String where string_non_empty`, ...). These are the `where_refinements_retire_for_checked_constructors` target."),
      li(text: "(b) bare transparent aliases that are nicknames (RHS a single bare carrier name): about 104, e.g. `type CommitSha = String`, `type Sha256 = String`, `type Email = String`, `type SemVer = String`, `type Bit = Bool`, `type UInt = Nat`. These are `single_authority` nicknaming."),
      li(text: "(c) bare aliases that are legitimate abbreviations of a parameterized type (RHS carries `<`): about 238, e.g. `type MoneyPerGibibyteHour = MoneyRate<PerGibibyteHour>`, `type InventoryLotIdentity = MintedId<InventoryLotSubject>`. These are KEPT -- they abbreviate, they do not nickname a kernel carrier and they do not claim a guarantee."),
      li(text: "(d) Compose/phantom forms: about 27, e.g. `type Compose<A, M> = Phantom`. These are governed by `machine_width_composition_has_an_intersection_carrier` and are NOT read as transparent aliases."),
    ]),
    p(text: "The cut therefore does NOT touch (c) or (d) as a class: refusing a parameterized abbreviation or collapsing the intersection carrier would be wrong and would collide with `machine_width_composition_has_an_intersection_carrier`. The interchangeability being refused is base<->derived at a check, which is a property of (a) and (b), not of abbreviation."),
    h2(text: "4. Checked constructors already present vs owed"),
    p(text: "Where-refinements that have a declared checked constructor returning Optional already, and so need only their `where` removed: `std.types` `checked_port(n: Int) -> Port?`, `checked_int_to_epoch_secs(n: Int) -> EpochSecs?`, plus checked forms for ByteSize, Sha256Digest, and Nat. The hottest types have NONE: `NonEmptyStr`, `PathSegment`, `FilePath`, `CommitSha` have no `-> X?` checked constructor, and construction today runs through the `as` coercion -- about 28826 `as NonEmptyStr`, 1332 `as FilePath`, 221 `as CommitSha`, 23 `as PathSegment` uses across the corpus. Those counts are the migration surface for steps 2 and 3, and the literal-only interim admission (`literal_only_refinement_judgment_is_interim`) is what lets a string literal into a refinement position today."),
    h2(text: "5. Cut order (consistent with replacement_migration and root_generalization)"),
    p(text: "Root_generalization failure example (a) is precisely this family: alias identity is decided by per-call-site fallbacks (`transparent_alias_identity_agrees` bolted onto individual sites in v1 04_types) instead of one rule with the symbol table; each teaching of one site broke another. replacement_migration says the old authority ends in one motion at its root and the new one never falls back to it. So the order is: put the ONE root decision first with a discriminating RED, then retire each ruled form, then the nicknames -- never a per-site admission."),
    ol(items: [
      li(text: "**Step 1 -- one root inhabitance decision at the argument, with the discriminating RED.** A single rule in v2 04_infer (`v2.std.inhabitance` application obligation check, where `application_argument_does_not_inhabit` already refuses distinct nominal widths and generic mismatches) is the authority for base<->derived; it must carry the symbol table so alias/refinement/nominal identity is decided once, not per site. Discriminating RED: a probe suite that passes `String`-at-`NonEmptyStr`, `String`-at-brand, `String`-at-nickname, `String`-at-`nominal_opaque` and refuses each, with controls (base at base, derived at derived, a distinct record, `Int` at `String`) unchanged. v2 is the frontier; v1 seed only mirrors it as the v2 parity gate. Size: one judgment plus its witness; the RED already exists in scratch."),
      li(text: "**Step 2 -- NonEmptyStr as a nominal reached by a checked constructor.** Author `non_empty_str(s: String) -> NonEmptyStr?` (and literal admission at the expected type, replacing the literal-only interim rule), remove `type NonEmptyStr = String where string_non_empty`, and migrate the `as NonEmptyStr` surface (the variable cases; the literal cases take the literal rule). Boundary: v2 frontier; std types move, and the v1 seed std is a parity mirror -- a seed std change is admitted only where it advances v2 self-host (the `gunbc.v1.v1_maintenance_standing::v1_seed_standing` purpose test), and teaching the seed a new refusal for its own sake is refused as SeedFeatureCompletion. Size: LARGE -- about 28826 `as NonEmptyStr` sites, though most are literals absorbed by the literal rule."),
      li(text: "**Step 3 -- the brands.** For each ruled brand, give it a checked constructor and remove the `where brand(...)`, starting where a constructor is cheap and call sites are few (PathSegment about 23 `as` sites, then CommitSha about 221, then FilePath about 1332), and finish the widths whose `where range(...) brand(...)` forms already have a checked conversion. Boundary: v2 frontier, std data + per-site migrations. Size: MEDIUM each, large in aggregate."),
      li(text: "**Step 4 -- the nickname aliases.** Retire (b) by naming the one authority each stands for, moving call sites to it; a bare rename of a kernel carrier is no longer a declaration form. This is `single_authority` (nicknaming), applied at the root, and it ends only after the interchangeability in step 1 is refused so no call site is quietly relying on the collapse. Boundary: v2 frontier, std + corpus. Size: MEDIUM; bounded by about 104 nickname headers and their call sites."),
    ]),
    h2(text: "6. Deliberately not in scope"),
    ul(items: [
      li(text: "Class (c) parameterized-abbreviation aliases and class (d) Compose/phantom forms stay; collapsing them is refused by `machine_width_composition_has_an_intersection_carrier` and they claim no guarantee."),
      li(text: "The literal-only interim admission is kept until step 2's expected-type literal introduction replaces it; it is what keeps string literals flowing today (`literal_only_refinement_judgment_is_interim`, rung_drop `literal_only_where_refinement_judgment`)."),
      li(text: "This intention adds no ruling; a blanket \"no aliases\" is explicitly not asserted."),
    ]),
    h2(text: "7. Evidence and the bounds of what is known"),
    ul(items: [
      li(text: "Probe suite: `probe.alias_interchange` (scratch, `gunbc.compile_diagnostic_census` on the v1 CompileAccept path, one `gunbc run --claim-run` process). Plain mismatches refuse; base-at-derived (where-refinement / brand / nickname / nominal_opaque) produce zero blocking rows; controls clean. Seed binary built release from this checkout."),
      li(text: "Counts: `grep -rE '^type [A-Za-z_]' dag/ src/v2/ --include=*.dag` header-line classification with precedence (where first, then Compose/phantom, then a `<` RHS, then a bare-identifier RHS). Per-class: about 326 where (284 branded / 42 predicate), 379 bare split into about 238 parameterized / about 104 nickname / about 27 Compose-phantom / about 10 other (function-type and qualified-path aliases)."),
      li(text: "UNKNOWN, stated: the counts are header-line grep, not a resolution census (multi-line headers, and `nominal_opaque`/`sole_constructor` markers are not separately tallied); the v2 real-path String-at-NonEmptyStr verdict is OWED (the same recurring_failure_mode row records the v2 claim as owed, citable only over two-declaration stand-ins); the split of the 28826 `as NonEmptyStr` sites into literal versus variable is not measured and bounds step 2's true cost."),
    ]),
    h2(text: "8. Realization"),
    p(text: "The steps of section 5 are realized as work items under the roadmap in `gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_authority`, each bound to this intention at its layer in `gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_intention_binding`, so a landing is read against the guarantee it serves: which derived type moved from interchangeable to refused at the argument, which `where`-refinement lost its predicate to a checked constructor, or which nickname lost its second name -- never a count of files rewritten."),
  ]
}

data derived_types_keep_their_name_plan: Plan = Plan {
  projection: PlanIsAuthorityOnly,
  slug: "derived-types-keep-their-name",
  title: "Derived types keep their name: refined, branded and nickname types stop standing in for their base, and where-refinements retire to checked constructors",
  body: derived_types_keep_their_name_body(),
  retirement: PlanRetiresWhen { condition: unbound_dissolution(description: "Section 1 is achieved: no where-refinement in the language, every derived type reached by a checked constructor or carried evidence, no bare nickname of a kernel carrier, and the one root inhabitance rule refusing base at a derived-type position with its discriminating RED green.") },
}
